"""Document-start detector for layers.1.mlp.down_proj:4049.

What it does: this component is nearly silent inside a document. It fires on the first
token of a document (the token right after <|endoftext|>, or the first token of a packed
row). There the model sees only that token, so the activation depends only on which token
it is. The program gives each kind of opening token a value:
  - a given first name (no leading space), a greeting (Hello, Hi, Welcome...), a yes/no
    or wh- question word (Is, Are, Why...), a month, or a common opening word (Here, Now,
    Today, Home, Black...): strongly positive;
  - a code opener (import, #!/): positive;
  - a single capital letter, or a capitalised run of one repeated letter (MMMM): positive;
  - another capitalised word: mildly positive;
  - an article, preposition, pronoun or determiner (the, on, in, your, you...): negative;
  - lower-case word pieces, digits and whitespace: slightly negative.
The values were set by hand, then refitted by least squares on sampled rows. Everywhere
else (all tokens after the first of a document) it predicts 0: those small values are not
modelled here.
"""

READS = ()

NAMES = set("""James John Robert Michael William David Richard Joseph Thomas Charles Christopher
Daniel Matthew Anthony Mark Donald Steven Paul Andrew Kenneth Kevin Brian George Edward Jason
Jeffrey Ryan Jacob Gary Eric Jonathan Justin Scott Brandon Benjamin Samuel Frank Peter Adam
Henry Jack Jerry Dennis Carl Bob Tom Jim Tim Dave Don Ron Ed Ted Fred Max Sam Ben Dan Mike Greg
Joe Bill Josh Mitch Gil Brad Luc Jan Jean Mary Patricia Jennifer Linda Elizabeth Barbara Susan
Jessica Sarah Karen Nancy Lisa Betty Sandra Emily Donna Carol Amanda Melissa Sharon Laura Amy
Anna Emma Helen Rachel Catherine Maria Julie Olivia Joy Beth Fran Alice Jane Lucy Eva Mia Ella
Sophia Grace Amber Diana Natalie Kim Ann Jim""".split())
GREETINGS = set("Hello Hi Hey Welcome Yes Sure Oh Ok Okay Well Wow".split())
QUESTION_OPENERS = set("""Is Are Was Were Does Did Do Will Would Should Has Have Can Could May
Why When Where""".split())
TIME_PLACE = set("Here Now Today Home Time New Black Green".split())
MONTHS = set("Jan Feb Mar Apr May Jun Jul Aug Sep Oct Nov Dec January February March April June July August September October November December".split())
FUNCTION_WORDS = set("""The On In For To At An Your You This These Their His Its They If With
Of From By And Or But What""".split())
CODE_OPENERS = {"import": 4.5, "#!/": 4.5}


def is_repeated_run(word):
    return len(word) >= 3 and word.isalpha() and len(set(word)) == 1


def value(s):
    """The activation predicted for a document's first token, given its text `s`."""
    word = s.strip()
    if not word:
        return -0.2
    if word in CODE_OPENERS:
        return CODE_OPENERS[word]
    if word.isalpha() and word[0].isupper():
        if word in GREETINGS or word in QUESTION_OPENERS or word in TIME_PLACE or word in MONTHS:
            return 5.0
        if word in NAMES:
            return 6.0 if s[0] != " " else 1.8
        if is_repeated_run(word):
            return 1.5
        if word in FUNCTION_WORDS:
            return -0.6
        if len(word) == 1 and s[0] != " ":
            return 2.0
        return 0.9
    if word.isdigit():
        return -0.3
    if s[0] == " ":
        return -0.4
    return -0.1


